{
  "text": " I'm saying it again. Prue looked at her own arms, and then at Kiva. Or didn't call that. You didn't call that either. We just both did it. She held up her bleeding fingertips. That's the first thing I've ever done in a lane that wasn't on somebody's word. Kiva looked at her. She thought of the yard behind the long key on Sunday, and Pike saying from a tailboard, you call from the air before you've landed, and Prue on a seating floor calling, hands off, left, before the tarn's carry had moved. It wasn't on anybody's, she said. That's why it worked.",
